      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How do I verify Bangladesh clothing manufacturer certifications?</h3>
        <p style="color:#ccc;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Request current certificate copies and verify them through the issuing organization's database (GOTS.org, Oeko-Tex.com, BSCI.org, Sedex.com). Legitimate manufacturers will provide valid certificates with expiration dates.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What are the payment terms for Bangladesh garment factories?</h3>
        <p style="color:#ccc;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Standard payment terms are 30% deposit to start production, 70% before shipment. Established factories may accept L/C (Letter of Credit) for large orders. Never pay 100% upfront.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How long does shipping from Bangladesh take?</h3>
        <p style="color:#ccc;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Ocean freight to EU/UK takes 20-30 days, to USA takes 25-35 days, to Australia takes 30-40 days. Air freight reduces this to 5-7 days but costs significantly more. Production adds 30-45 days before shipping.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What is the difference between FOB and CIF pricing?</h3>
        <p style="color:#ccc;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">FOB (Free On Board) covers costs up to the port in Bangladesh. CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) includes shipping to your destination port. Most Bangladesh manufacturers quote FOB Chittagong or Dhaka.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

